    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106">

                <pb facs="0190" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg144"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.61311/-</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">2 September, 1918</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: This action on the part
                    of Lord Reading is certainly very courteous and very right and I appreciate
                        it.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d106-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I am, however, of the same judgment as Mr. Hoover. There can be no just objection
                    on our part to any such action as the British Government has in mind with regard
                    to the price of their own domestic wheat.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
